Caelza: the looks and the shop (vision M8), every agent's pixel character.

An agent was a bot icon. Now it has a character: one piece per layer
(backdrop, body, outfit, hair, hat, face, accessory) in the owner's colours,
drawn as code in looks/parts.py, composed and recoloured in the browser
(web/src/looks/Look.tsx over the exported PNGs under web/public/looks), kept
on the Runtime per agent so every device shows the same. The customizer
(/looks/:alias), the gallery (/looks) and the shop of packs (/shop) are
overlay pages; the gateway's api_looks.rs is an overlay module. These hunks
register the module and its routes (/api/looks/wardrobe, /api/looks/{alias}),
route the pages, put Looks and Shop in the sidebar's Chat group and the
title maps, add the API client functions, draw the look in the agent card
and the chat (the header's talks while the agent answers), add the strings
(English; the other locales fall back) and list the logic test beside the
others. Applied after 0010 and the overlay copy.

